<title>USA: U.S. deficit expected to decline to about $36 bln.</title>
<headline>U.S. deficit expected to decline to about $36 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton is expected to announce Wednesday that the U.S. budget deficit for the current fiscal year has declined further to about $36 billion, an administration official said.</p>
<p>The new estimate of a further dramatic decline in deficit spending, evidence of a booming economy and surging tax revenues, came only a week after White House budget director Franklin Raines said the budget deficit for fiscal 1997 would be below $50 billion.</p>
</text>
